* Component Created by Javier Petrucci and Agustin Gullino
* jpetrucc@itba.edu.ar / agullino@itba.edu.ar
*
* This is the NPN BJT
*
*         C
*     |  /
*     | /
* B---|
*     | \
*     | _\|
*          E
*
*
*  /\Ic
*  |
*  |
*  |        /--------------------
*  |       /
*  |      /----------------------
*  |     /
*  |    /------------------------
*  |   /
*  |  /--------------------------
*  | /
*  |/__________________________________> Vbe
*
*
* Behaviour:
*   - Vbe is clamped to {Vbe} whenever the BE junction is forward biased
*   - Ic = hfe * Ib   exactly, in the forward active region
*   - Vce is clamped to {Vsat} in saturation
*   - reverse active region works with a beta of hfe/rbeta
*
* Note on Vsat: Vce = Vbe - Vbc is an identity, so clamping Vce at {Vsat}
* while Vbe is clamped at {Vbe} forces the BC junction to turn on at
* {Vbe-Vsat}. That single diode is therefore both the BC junction and the
* saturation clamp -- having two separate elements fight over the same
* voltage is what made the previous version of this model hard to solve.
*
* Note on convergence: every element below is linear except the two diodes,
* so the Jacobian is constant apart from two entries. There are no behavioural
* sources, no division by a node voltage or by a branch current, and no
* limit()/abs(), all of which have zero or undefined derivatives exactly at
* the cutoff and saturation operating points. epsilon/revepsilon round the
* diode knees so Newton always has a continuous gradient to follow, and the
* junction capacitances break the otherwise purely algebraic feedback loop
* in transient analysis.

.SUBCKT NPN_nice C B E PARAMS: hfe=100 Vbe=0.7 Vsat=0.3 rbeta=20 cje=2p cjc=1p droff=1G dron=10m deps=10m


**Base emitter junction: fixes Vbe, and its current is the base current
Vf  B  Nf  0
Dbe Nf E   Dbe_mod

**Base collector junction: fixes Vce at {Vsat} in saturation by taking the
**collector current the external circuit cannot supply out of the base
Vr  B  Nr  0
Dbc Nr C   Dbc_mod

**Forward transport: Ic = hfe * Ib, an exact linear current gain
Ff  C  E   Vf {hfe}

**Reverse transport, with a beta of hfe/rbeta
Fr  E  C   Vr {hfe/rbeta}

**Junction capacitances, needed so the transport loop is not purely algebraic
Cbe B  E   {cje}
Cbc B  C   {cjc}


**Models for the diodes
.model Dbe_mod D(Ron={dron} Roff={droff} Vfwd={Vbe}      epsilon={deps} revepsilon={deps})
.model Dbc_mod D(Ron={dron} Roff={droff} Vfwd={Vbe-Vsat} epsilon={deps} revepsilon={deps})

.ends NPN_nice
